    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0270" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Air Armaments/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation
                            (Gibson) to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-31T22:00:00+01:00">May 31, 1932—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 31—9:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>224. In connection with the work of the Air Commission it is quite likely that
                    proposals will be presented respecting adoption of rules to control aerial
                    warfare. In view of this we would appreciate learning from Department whether
                    report of the Commission of Jurists which met at The Hague in 1923<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d97-f1"/> constitutes a satisfactory basis for elaboration of such
                    rules and if so would appreciate by mail any detailed suggestions with respect
                    to this report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
